my/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-11+8\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/d3b5558c0268843618c52c588ffcf1c8012189041b17d52fadd6fe74c3526700.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{11} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\frac{8}{11}) \\\\  & =0.628\\text{ }796\\text{ }…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi -0.628\\text{ }796\\text{ }…≈2.51,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "59830984d11c84f433473922c52bfca2dd9f8745ba91fa00a054f7687658f69a" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319499" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319499" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.51"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=-5+5\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/f466a110eda3b07b50d988de6e46a541ad85d7ff64f43a6f056ea216752fa2d9.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{5} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "59830984d11c84f433473922c52bfca2dd9f8745ba91fa00a054f7687658f69a" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/state.json" "file_sha256" "9186a80455cc68616a01432300a59c7e5bf3759d89dd60e1f6e0e48abb1eb896" "basis" 320 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=8-11\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal 